    historical_tag: Some("The Salt Fork of the Red River was a strategic crossing point in the Texas Panhandle, used by both the U.S. Army and Native warriors during the Red River War and its aftermath. By the summer of 1875, most major hostilities had ended, but scattered skirmishes continued as the last free bands were hunted down or forced onto reservations."),
